# Special Tags Test

Tests special tags: #id, #dep, #group-start, #group-due, @person, #done.


## ID and Dependency Tags

[ ] Task with unique ID #id:task-001
[ ] Task depending on task-001 #dep:task-001
[ ] Another dependent task #dep:task-001
[ ] Task with UUID #id:7d444840-9dc0-11d1-b245-5ffdce74fad2
[ ] Orphaned dependency (no matching ID) #dep:nonexistent-id


## Group Start Tag

[ ] Project A #group-start:2026-03-01
    [ ] Subtask 1 (covered by the parent's #group-start)
    [ ] Subtask 2 (covered by the parent's #group-start)
    [ ] Subtask 3 (covered by the parent's #group-start)


## Group Due Tag

[ ] Project B #group-due:2026-06-30
    [ ] Subtask 1 (covered by the parent's #group-due)
    [ ] Subtask 2 (covered by the parent's #group-due)
    [ ] Subtask 3 (covered by the parent's #group-due)


## Combined Group Tags

[ ] Project C #group-start:2026-04-01 #group-due:2026-09-30
    /// The parent's tags give the start and due date of the whole group,
    /// so the subtasks need no dates of their own.
    [ ] Design phase
    [ ] Implementation phase
    [ ] Testing phase


## Person/Location Tags (@person)

[ ] Review code @john
[ ] Meeting @mary @office
[ ] Buy supplies @store
[ ] Call client @john-doe
[ ] Visit site @tokyo @japan


## Done Tag

[x] Completed task #done:2026-02-15
[x] Completed with timestamp #done:2026-02-15_14:30:00
[x] Completed with unixtime #done:1739635200
[~] Cancelled task #done:2026-02-14


## Complex Combinations

[ ] Complex task #id:complex-001 #group-start:2026-03-01 #group-due:2026-06-30
    [ ] Subtask A @john #dep:complex-001
    [ ] Subtask B @mary 2026-04-01 -> 2026-05-01
    [x] Subtask C completed #done:2026-02-15_10:00:00


## Sequential Tasks (#seq-tasks)

Each child can start only after the previous sibling is done or cancelled.

[@] Sequential parent #seq-tasks
    [x] Step 1 (done, so step 2 is ready)
    [ ] Step 2 (ready)
    [ ] Step 3 (blocked by step 2)
    [ ] Step 4 (blocked by step 3)

[ ] Not sequential: #seq-tasks-like is a different tag, not #seq-tasks
    [ ] Child A
    [ ] Child B
